/F2 16 Tf (AHU-200 Air Handling Unit - Maintenance Manual) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (1. About this manual) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Synthetic reference text written for the AlixAI facility-maintenance reference application.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (No real equipment is described.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (The AHU-200 is a single-duct air handling unit with a supply fan, a return filter bank, a) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (heating coil and a cooling coil.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (2. Safety) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Isolate and lock out the unit at the local disconnect before opening any access panel.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Wait 5 minutes after isolation for the fan motor capacitor to discharge.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Wear gloves when handling filters: they hold dust and mould spores.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (3. Routine maintenance schedule) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Weekly: check the filter differential pressure display and the condensate drain for) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  blockage.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Monthly: check the supply fan belt tension and look for cracks or glazing on the belt.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Quarterly: replace the pleated return filter \(part FLT-204\) every 3 months, or earlier) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  when the differential pressure exceeds 250 Pa.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- Annually: clean both coils, check the damper linkages and test the freeze protection) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  thermostat.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (4. Fault codes) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- E01 Supply fan overload: check the belt tension, the motor current and the bearings.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- E04 Filter alarm: the differential pressure across the filter bank is above 250 Pa.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  Replace the filters \(FLT-204\).) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- E07 Coil freeze protection: the coil air temperature fell below 3 C. Check the heating) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  valve and the outside air damper.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- E09 Return air damper fault: the damper did not reach its position within 90 seconds.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (  Check the actuator and the linkage.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (5. Replacing the supply fan belt) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (Use a V-belt B-section 1180 mm \(part BLT-11\). Loosen the motor base bolts, remove the old) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (belt, fit the new belt and tension it until a firm thumb press at the middle of the span) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (deflects it by 10 mm. Tighten the bolts and run the fan for 10 minutes, then re-check the) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (tension.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (A new belt stretches during its first hours of running: re-check the tension after 24 hours) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (of operation.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13.5 Tf (6. Parts) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- FLT-204 Pleated air filter 592x592, quantity per change: 2.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- BLT-11 V-belt B-section 1180 mm, quantity per change: 1.) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf (- CAP-45 Run capacitor 45 uF for the supply fan motor.) Tj T*
T*
